# USB runtime power management: OFF.
#
# A PBX with USB GSM modems must never autosuspend the bus. The kernel default
# here is usbcore.autosuspend=2 (two idle seconds), and a suspend/resume cycle
# on a Huawei modem can drop or re-enumerate the device right after a call when
# its serial ports go idle. This rule pins power/control="on" for every USB
# device, which is vendor- and model-agnostic, so it holds on any server.
#
# Do not weaken it back to "auto": the file name is the contract.
ACTION=="add", SUBSYSTEM=="usb", ENV{DEVTYPE}=="usb_device", ATTR{power/control}="on"
